<body>

<h1>SAP Fleet Management Add-on: Interview Demo Documentation</h1>

<h2>1. Master Data Management</h2>

<h3>1.1 Vehicle Master</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Core Identity:</strong> Captures primary vehicle identification such as Vehicle Code, Registration Number, VIN, Engine Number, and Category/Type.</li>
  <li><strong>Make &amp; Model Tracking:</strong> Stores manufacturer details including Make, Model, Variant, Year of Manufacture, Color, and Asset Tags.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical Specifications:</strong> Records engine capacity (cc), maximum power/torque, emission standards, fuel type, transmission, and drive layout.</li>
  <li><strong>Physical &amp; Load Capacity:</strong> Details vehicle dimensions, gross vehicle weight, payload capacity, wheelbase, and fuel/AdBlue tank capacity.</li>
  <li><strong>Lifecycle Management:</strong> Includes dedicated tabs to track ownership, insurance, daily operations, maintenance, tyres, batteries, and compliance documents.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.2 Tyre Master</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Unique Identification:</strong> Registers each tyre individually using a unique Tyre ID and Serial Number for asset tracking.</li>
  <li><strong>Brand &amp; Build Specs:</strong> Captures brand, model, size, and ply rating to ensure the correct tyre fits the appropriate vehicle.</li>
  <li><strong>Procurement Details:</strong> Records purchase document numbers, purchase dates, and item costs directly in the system.</li>
  <li><strong>Warranty Tracking:</strong> Monitors warranty terms in both running kilometers (KM) and elapsed months.</li>
  <li><strong>Lifecycle Status:</strong> Maintains the operational status of the tyre (e.g., in-use, spare, retreaded, or scrapped).</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.3 Permit / Insurance Master</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Vehicle Mapping:</strong> Links permits and insurance policies directly to the specific Vehicle Number/Code.</li>
  <li><strong>Policy &amp; Permit Records:</strong> Captures permit types, permit numbers, policy numbers, and insurance coverage levels.</li>
  <li><strong>Insurer &amp; Cost:</strong> Records the assigned insurance company (insurer) and the recurring premium amounts paid.</li>
  <li><strong>Validity Dates:</strong> Stores the "Valid From" and "Valid To" timeline for each official certificate.</li>
  <li><strong>Renewal Alerts:</strong> Tracks the next renewal date to prevent lapses, avoid legal penalties, and ensure fleet compliance.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Operations &amp; Dispatch</h2>

<h3>2.1 Trip Plan</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Core Assignment:</strong> Links the designated vehicle, assigned driver, co-driver, route, and target customer for the journey.</li>
  <li><strong>Schedule &amp; Timeline:</strong> Captures planned start and end times, document date, trip purpose, and estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li>
  <li><strong>Route Leg Planning:</strong> Breaks the journey down row-by-row with individual legs, specifying each "From Location" and "To Location".</li>
  <li><strong>Cost &amp; Fuel Estimation:</strong> Estimates total operational metrics per leg, including planned kilometers, transit duration, toll fees, and fuel requirements in liters.</li>
  <li><strong>Documentation &amp; Billing:</strong> Associates critical shipping references such as Invoice PDF, Manifest, and Delivery Order (DO) numbers for full traceability.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Fuel Management</h2>

<h3>3.1 Fuel Issue</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Trip &amp; Vehicle Linking:</strong> Connects fuel dispensing directly to a specific Trip Number, Vehicle Code, Fuel Station, and Fuel Type.</li>
  <li><strong>Commercial Accounting:</strong> Records fuel quantity (in liters), unit rate, total bill amount, vendor code (BP Code), payment mode, and invoice/bill number.</li>
  <li><strong>Mileage Calculation:</strong> Captures the current odometer reading to automatically calculate fuel efficiency (KMPL).</li>
  <li><strong>Fraud &amp; Error Prevention:</strong> Features built-in validations such as "Duplicate Bill Check" and a sanity check comparing current vs. previous odometer readings.</li>
  <li><strong>SAP Inventory Posting:</strong> Directly integrates with SAP Business One backend transactions via the "Posting" button to update stock and ledger entries immediately.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Maintenance &amp; Garage</h2>

<h3>4.1 Preventive Maintenance</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Vehicle &amp; Service Rule:</strong> Links a vehicle code to a predefined PM (Preventive Maintenance) Code and tracking document.</li>
  <li><strong>Trigger Conditions:</strong> Defines the trigger type (such as distance or time) that signals when service is due.</li>
  <li><strong>Threshold &amp; Grace Limits:</strong> Configures exact trigger thresholds along with allowable grace limits before triggering an alert.</li>
  <li><strong>Standard BOM Kits:</strong> Attaches standard parts kits (Bill of Materials) required for the scheduled maintenance cycle.</li>
  <li><strong>Labor &amp; Time Estimates:</strong> Sets standard labor costs and expected service completion hours for budgeting and planning.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2 Work Order</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Issue Reporting:</strong> Captures the reporting person, reported complaint, confirmed diagnosis, and repair priority.</li>
  <li><strong>SLA &amp; Timeline:</strong> Records the work order open date and close date to monitor garage turnaround time.</li>
  <li><strong>Task &amp; Part Breakdown:</strong> Uses a line-item matrix to track individual repair tasks along with required spare parts.</li>
  <li><strong>Labor Tracking:</strong> Details specific technician or labor allocations assigned to each repair item.</li>
  <li><strong>Cost Variance Analysis:</strong> Compares estimated repair costs against actual incurred costs directly per task line.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.3 Breakdown Log &amp; Tow</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Incident Logging:</strong> Records on-road breakdown incidents with vehicle number, failure location, and breakdown fault code.</li>
  <li><strong>Corrective Measures:</strong> Documents immediate action taken on-site, including towing or emergency repairs.</li>
  <li><strong>Downtime Monitoring:</strong> Captures non-operational downtime hours to assess vehicle availability loss.</li>
  <li><strong>Vendor &amp; Expense Tracking:</strong> Records the recovery or service vendor (BP Code) and the associated breakdown/towing costs.</li>
  <li><strong>Operational Traceability:</strong> Includes a "Trip Link" reference to tie the roadside breakdown directly back to an active dispatch trip.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Tyre Lifecycle Management</h2>

<h3>5.1 Fit / Rotate / Remove</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Action Tracking:</strong> Records specific operational tyre movements, whether fitting a new tyre, rotating positions, or removing one.</li>
  <li><strong>Position &amp; Vehicle Mapping:</strong> Maps the specific Tyre ID directly to a Vehicle Number/Code and its exact Axle Position.</li>
  <li><strong>Wear &amp; Condition Inspection:</strong> Captures vital physical parameters during changes, specifically current Tread Depth and tyre Pressure.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage Benchmark:</strong> Records the current Odometer reading to track the exact kilometers run on that specific axle position.</li>
  <li><strong>Documentation &amp; Notes:</strong> Generates system document numbers and dates while allowing technicians to enter custom inspection remarks.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.2 Retread &amp; Scrap</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Vendor &amp; Service Cost:</strong> Details the external Retread Vendor and records the direct cost incurred for extending tyre life.</li>
  <li><strong>Spec Restoration:</strong> Records the renewed Tread Depth achieved after the retreading process.</li>
  <li><strong>Warranty Adjustment:</strong> Allows a "Warranty Reset" value to update and restart the tracking lifecycle for retreaded tyres.</li>
  <li><strong>End-of-Life Disposal:</strong> Captures the specific "Scrap Reason" when a tyre is damaged beyond repair or reaches end-of-life.</li>
  <li><strong>Financial Recovery:</strong> Tracks the Scrap Residual Value to ensure accurate financial write-offs and scrap sales accounting.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Compliance &amp; Safety</h2>

<h3>6.1 Renewal &amp; Alerts</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Core Document Tracking:</strong> Centralizes statutory document dates including Insurance, Permit, Fitness, PUC, and FASTag KYC.</li>
  <li><strong>System Numbering:</strong> Automatically generates a system Document Number and logs the active Document Date.</li>
  <li><strong>Compliance Management:</strong> Helps fleet managers monitor document expirations across vehicles from a single screen.</li>
  <li><strong>Proactive Notification:</strong> Serves as the tracking foundation to set renewal alerts and prevent vehicle impoundment or route disruptions.</li>
  <li><strong>Penalty Prevention:</strong> Ensures timely certificate renewals to prevent regulatory non-compliance fines.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.2 Challans / Fines</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Vehicle &amp; Driver Mapping:</strong> Directly maps a traffic penalty or violation to both the specific Vehicle and the Driver responsible.</li>
  <li><strong>Violation Details:</strong> Records the issuing Authority, Violation Type (e.g., speeding, overloading), Incident Date, and Violation Location.</li>
  <li><strong>Financial Tracking:</strong> Captures the fine Amount due to monitor penalty expenses and support payroll deductions or vendor settlements.</li>
  <li><strong>Settlement Status:</strong> Tracks current payment progress using the Status dropdown (e.g., Pending, Contested, or Paid).</li>
  <li><strong>Document Attachment:</strong> Provides a dedicated Documents link/attachment field to upload scanned digital copies of physical challan receipts.</li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>